# Baseline for tests\autotest\run_resolver_version_guard.ps1
#
# <DRAGLINT_RESOLVER_VERSION>|<sha256 of the resolve surface>
#
# The resolve surface is the set of routines listed in tests\resolver-surface.txt
# -- the code that DERIVES call_edges, type_ancestors, type_helpers and
# unit_uses targets from parses the index already holds. Change any of it and
# this guard fails until DRAGLINT_RESOLVER_VERSION is bumped, because every
# existing index would otherwise keep edges from the OLD resolver.
#
# THE REMEDY IS CHEAP, and that is the whole point of a second stamp. A bump of
# DRAGLINT_EXTRACTOR_VERSION costs a ~5 hour re-parse of every database; a bump
# of THIS one costs a re-resolve measured in minutes. They were conflated until
# 2026-08-31, which over-billed 19 commits under src\index and under-billed 42
# under src\storage -- the latter going silently stale, one every 2.2 days.
#
# EXACTLY ONE ACTIVE LINE. The sibling extractor baseline was APPENDED to rather
# than replaced on 2026-08-26 and its guard, which reads only the first active
# line, became structurally incapable of failing for five days. This guard
# asserts its own baseline's shape for that reason. Move superseded lines into
# `#` history below.
#
# To update: bump the constant in src\core\DRagLint.Core.Model.pas, re-run the
# guard, paste the line it prints. If a change genuinely cannot affect what is
# derived, update the hash WITHOUT bumping and say why here -- the same
# discipline the extractor baseline uses, and the same warning: the failure mode
# of getting it wrong is SILENT.
#
# 2026-08-31: created. Seeded at 1.0.0-alpha rather than mirroring the extractor
#   version, because this stamp has its own history from here and pretending it
#   shares the extractor's past would be false. Existing indexes carry no
#   resolver_fingerprint at all and are grandfathered by the same rule the
#   indexer fingerprint uses -- an absent stamp adopts the current one silently
#   rather than forcing a mass re-resolve on first run.

# 2026-08-31: 1.0.0-alpha -> 1.1.0-alpha. UpsertCallEdge now writes
#   refs.symbol_id for a CERTAIN call edge, and ClearCallEdges nulls the column
#   it wrote. That column has been NULL on every row of every index while
#   INDEX-SCHEMA.md documented a join on it, so every consumer of `refs` was
#   name-joining whether it meant to or not. This is a genuine change to what
#   the resolve pass DERIVES, so every index owes one re-resolve -- minutes,
#   not the ~5 hours a re-parse would cost, which is the entire reason this
#   stamp is separate from DRAGLINT_EXTRACTOR_VERSION.
#
#   Superseded: 1.0.0-alpha|ae753fb79518fac5b932d8e9f6d78fc0fce625248ae44c846ac4ae6a57b805be

